  body: |
    # Negligible work in the source’s ESA guidance

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes a prior question of whether a very small amount of work is negligible, considering normal duties, effort and the contribution to a business.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 41145–41147 do not create a universal hours threshold or a blanket self-employment exemption. Material running, supervision or administration of a business is distinguished from negligible activity; facts and case law remain necessary.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 41145, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=38)
    - [DMG 41146, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=38)
    - [DMG 41147, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=38)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

